# JOURNAL FORMAT — journal.jsonl

`ledger/journal.jsonl` is append-only. Correct a bad record with a new event; never delete history.

## Base record

```json
{"ts":"<ISO8601>","event":"<type>","unit":"<id|null>","detail":"<summary>","verdict":"<pass|fail|null>","evidence":"<raw evidence path>","cost":{"tokens":0,"seconds":0,"retries":0}}
```

Read legacy string `cost` values for compatibility, but write new cost as an aggregatable object. Add a stable key and response grade to failures.

```json
{"event":"fail","key":"<category:subtype>","grade":"R|S","escalated":false}
```

Do not count an escalation record as a second incident.

## Events

| Event | When |
|---|---|
| `session_start`, `session_end` | Session boundary |
| `unit_start`, `unit_done` | Work-unit boundary |
| `eval` | Task-evaluator verdict |
| `fail`, `recovery`, `recovery_exhausted` | Failure and recovery |
| `checkpoint`, `decision`, `feedback` | State or decision boundary |
| `trigger_check` | Deterministic `none|targeted|full` decision |
| `harness_eval` | Baseline/control/treatment report |
| `improve_proposed`, `improve_accepted`, `improve_rejected` | Harness-candidate lifecycle |

## Rules

- An unrecorded evaluation did not happen.
- Aggregate with scripts; do not load the full journal into LLM context.
- Track operating cost separately from harness-evaluation cost.
- Never send harness history outside this project automatically.
